+# Implementation Tasks: Threshold Evaluation
+
+- [x] Add `--threshold` option parsing to frai-cli eval command
+- [x] Implement threshold validation (format check, metric ID check, value range 0-1)
+- [x] Add `thresholds` parameter to `generateReport` in frai-core
+- [x] Implement threshold evaluation logic in `generateReport`
+- [x] Update JSON report format with `passed` field and `thresholds` array
+- [x] Update Markdown report format with "Thresholds" section
+- [x] Implement exit code logic in runEvalCommand (exit 0/1/2)
+- [x] Handle metrics with null scores (should fail their thresholds)
+- [x] Add unit tests for threshold checking in frai-core
+- [x] Add JSDoc comments for generateReport function
+- [x] Validate metric IDs against evaluations results
+- [x] Document the `--threshold` option in CLI help
+- [x] Verify JSON output includes passed and thresholds
+- [x] Verify Markdown output includes Thresholds section
+- [x] Verify threshold logic with manual tests
+- [x] Clean up test files
+
+## Summary
+
+All tasks complete! The threshold feature has been fully implemented with:
+
+### frai-cli Changes
+- Added `--threshold <metric=min>` option (repeatable)
+- Validates threshold format (metric=number)
+- Validates threshold range (0-1)
+- Validates metric IDs against evaluations results
+- Exits with code 0 (pass), 1 (fail), or 2 (usage error)
+- Reports are always written before exit
+
+### frai-core Changes
+- `generateReport()` accepts optional `thresholds` parameter
+- Returns `passed: boolean` when thresholds specified
+- Returns `thresholds: array` with `{metric, min, score, passed}` per threshold
+- Metrics with null scores fail their thresholds
+- JSON format automatically includes these fields
+- Markdown format includes "Thresholds" section with PASS/FAIL status
+
+### Testing
+- Unit tests added for threshold evaluation
+- Manual testing verified correct behavior
+- All report formats (JSON, Markdown) verified working
